# Frontend standards

> **Mobile**: this project has no native mobile client and no responsive-mobile-specific code path today (PatternFly's own responsive grid is the only adaptation). Treat this file as the baseline that would extend to a future mobile/React Native client (shared API contracts in `api/types.ts`, same error-message-extraction convention, same i18n key structure) if one is ever built.

## Structure

`components/` holds domain-grouped UI (`import/`, `history/`, `conversion/`, `connection/`, `api/`, `yaml/`) plus cross-cutting pieces (`AppStateContext`, `LangSwitcher`, `RouteErrorBoundary`). `pages/` are thin orchestrators (<200 lines target) that compose components, call APIs, and write via `useAppState()`. Pure logic without JSX lives in `components/<domain>/*Utils.ts` or `pages/*.ts` (`compatibilityChecks.ts`) so it can be tested without mounting. CSS Modules co-locate with components (`components/import/import.module.css`, etc.).

## Component conventions

- `const XxxPage: React.FC = (...) => {...}; export default XxxPage;` — orchestrator pages; `interface Props` only when a page still accepts props (most workflow pages use context only).
- Subcomponents under `components/<domain>/` with explicit prop boundaries; presentational pieces receive data/callbacks from the page orchestrator.
- State: local `useState` for form fields; workflow state via `useAppState()`. `useCallback` only for functions that are `useEffect` dependencies.
- API calls: `async/await` in **page orchestrators** (preferred), wrapped in `try/catch/finally`, with explicit `loading`/`error` state. One-shot UI-hint fetches (e.g. `clusterApi.getDomain()` for field prefill) may live in the component that triggers them when the result stays local and failure is silently acceptable.
- PatternFly 5 components only for UI chrome. Multi-step flow is plain routes + `navigate()` — no `Wizard`.

## API client (`api/client.ts` / `api/types.ts`)

- One Axios instance, base URL from `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || ''`. Request interceptor sets `Accept-Language` from `i18n.language`; response interceptor only clears the persisted connection on 401/403.
- No global `Authorization` header — pass `bearerHeaders(accessToken)` explicitly per call.
- Domain-grouped plain objects: `connectionApi`, `conversionApi`, `historyApi`, etc.
- `api/types.ts` = API contracts only. `AppState` lives in `components/AppStateContext.tsx`.

## Form validation

- No schema library (`zod`/`yup`). Manual `if` + boolean state; PatternFly `FormHelperText` preferred.
- Disable submit when invalid (`isDisabled={loading || !url}`).

## Error handling

- Use `apiErrorMessage(e, fallback)` from `utils/apiError.ts` with `catch (e: unknown)` in all pages.
- `components/RouteErrorBoundary` wraps `<Routes>` in `App.tsx`.

## State

`AppStateContext` + `useAppState()` replace prop drilling. Provider sits inside `BrowserRouter` in `App.tsx`. `utils/appStateStorage.ts` persists a **sanitized** subset to `sessionStorage` — never persist `accessToken` or `connected: true` without a live token (I-2/I-3).

## i18n

- `useTranslation()` + `t('page.key')`, nested keys (`connection.title`). Prefixes: `btnX`, `labelX`, `colX`, `errorX`, `ariaX`.
- Every key in `locales/en.json` must exist in `locales/ja.json` (`locales/locales.smoke.test.ts`).

## Styling

PatternFly utilities + CSS Modules co-located with components. Use `styles/pfTokens.ts` constants — no CSS-in-JS, Tailwind, or Sass.

## Naming

Files: PascalCase for components (`ConnectionForm.tsx`), camelCase for utils. Handlers: `handleX` in orchestrator, `onX` for props passed down.

## Suggested improvements (not yet implemented)

- Full `@testing-library/react` coverage for forms and wizards — [#172](https://github.com/Everything-is-Code/migration-toolkit-rhcl/issues/172).
- Backend unified error envelope once `@ServerExceptionMapper` lands ([#171](https://github.com/Everything-is-Code/migration-toolkit-rhcl/issues/171)).
